<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="med-lemon" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Mediterranean Lemon Soup</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>2 tablespoons butter</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 cup finely minced onion</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>1 cup cooked brown rice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup lemon juice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 cup vegetable stock</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 beaten eggs, room temperature</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon dried crushed mint</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a soup sized pan, saute the onion in butter with salt and pepper until the onion is soft and translucent.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add the rice, stock, and lemon juice.  Heat is covered, over a low flame until it boils gently.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Stir the soup rapidly as you drizzle in the beaten egg. Add mint; remove from heat.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>